  "articleBody": "Dividing a basement, adding a powder room, or reconfiguring a bedroom closet changes how your home functions. While partition walls look simple on the surface, several situations call for an experienced finish contractor to ensure the final space is built right.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps:\n- Coordinating Plumbing and Electrical Penetrations: Walls holding supply lines, shower valves, or dedicated electrical circuits need planned stud sizing and strategic blocking to avoid weakened framing.\n- Building Custom Closets, Niches, or Pocket Doors: Recessed shelving, pocket door frames, and specialized architectural openings demand rigid framing that will not rub or sag over time.\n- Installing Backing for Accessibility Grab Bars: Disability modifications and bathroom grab bars require specific solid wood blocking secured into adjacent framing to meet support demands.\n- Framing Over Uneven Slabs or Out-of-Level Ceilings: Basements and older homes often have sloped concrete floors or irregular joists that require scribed plates and custom stud lengths.\n- Preparing for High-End Tile and Trim: Surfaces receiving marble, tile, or detailed casing demand straight, plumb framing to prevent lippage and gaps.\n\nBringing in a skilled contractor keeps your interior partition project running efficiently from rough framing through final paint. Contact Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to plan your interior remodeling work.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}